@*
    The login artwork's emblem.

    Deliberately abstract. The approved reference is a photograph of a
    gold-striped tiger against a dark ground, and that file is not in this
    repository; committing an invented figurative stand-in would put fake brand
    artwork into source control, and a hand-drawn animal at this size reads as
    a cartoon rather than as the reference's restraint. What is drawn instead is
    the reference's actual visual signature - tapered gold striping raking
    across a dark field - which carries the same identity without pretending to
    be the photograph.

    The composition is built so the real asset drops in without a code change:
    place it at wwwroot/img/login-tiger.jpg and set --login-photo on .login__art
    (see tiger.css). It layers over this and neither the type nor the form moves.
*@
<svg class="login__emblem" viewBox="0 0 420 420" role="img" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
     preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
    <defs>
        <linearGradient id="tg-stripe" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#e3c46f" stop-opacity="0.85" />
            <stop offset="55%" stop-color="#c9a03c" stop-opacity="0.55" />
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#8a6718" stop-opacity="0.10" />
        </linearGradient>
        <linearGradient id="tg-stripe-faint" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#e3c46f" stop-opacity="0.28" />
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#8a6718" stop-opacity="0.04" />
        </linearGradient>
    </defs>

    @* Tapered strokes, raking from lower left to upper right. Each is a closed
       path rather than a stroked line so the taper is real. *@
    <g fill="url(#tg-stripe)">
        <path d="M56 300c46-58 96-112 150-160 8-7 17-13 26-19-6 10-14 20-23 29-46 47-91 96-131 152-8 11-16 22-22 34 0-13 0-25 0-36Z" />
        <path d="M120 328c50-62 104-121 162-173 9-8 19-15 29-22-7 11-15 21-25 31-49 51-97 104-140 162-9 12-17 24-25 37 0-12 0-24 0-35Z" />
        <path d="M196 348c48-60 100-117 156-167 9-8 18-15 28-21-7 10-15 20-24 30-47 49-94 100-135 156-9 12-17 24-25 36 0-12 0-23 0-34Z" />
    </g>

    <g fill="url(#tg-stripe-faint)">
        <path d="M20 232c40-50 84-97 131-140 7-6 15-12 23-17-6 9-13 18-20 26-40 41-79 84-114 132-7 9-14 19-20 29 0-11 0-21 0-30Z" />
        <path d="M268 366c44-54 91-106 142-152 8-7 17-14 26-20-6 9-14 19-22 27-43 45-86 92-124 143-8 11-15 22-22 33 0-11 0-21 0-31Z" />
        <path d="M338 388c34-42 71-82 111-118 6-6 13-11 20-16-5 7-11 15-17 21-34 35-68 72-98 112-6 8-12 17-16 25 0-8 0-16 0-24Z" />
    </g>

    @* A single hairline rule, the editorial device that keeps the field from
       looking like decoration for its own sake. *@
    <path d="M40 396h340" stroke="#d4ab45" stroke-opacity="0.30" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" />
</svg>
